[0m[31mI'll solve this step by step.
[0m[31m
[0m[31m## Problem Understanding
[0m[31m
[0m[31m1. We have a strip of n cells, each containing a direction ('>' or '<') and a jump length
[0m[31m2. Grasshopper starts at cell 0 (first cell)
[0m[31m3. From each cell i, it jumps according to the direction and length
[0m[31m4. If the grasshopper jumps outside the strip (to index < 0 or >= n), it stops
[0m[31m5. We need to determine if the grasshopper will eventually jump out (FINITE) or keep jumping forever (INFINITE)
[0m[31m
[0m[31m## Key Insight
[0m[31m
[0m[31mThe grasshopper will jump forever if it enters a cycle - it keeps visiting the same cells in a repeating pattern.
[0m[31m
[0m[31mIf the grasshopper jumps out of bounds, the answer is "FINITE".
[0m[31mIf the grasshopper keeps visiting cells in a cycle, the answer is "INFINITE".
[0m[31m
[0m[31m## Approach
[0m[31m
[0m[31m1. Simulate the grasshopper's movement step by step
[0m[31m2. Keep track of which cells we've visited
[0m[31m3. If we visit a cell we've seen before, we've entered a cycle → "INFINITE"
[0m[31m4. If we jump outside the bounds, we stop → "FINITE"
[0m[31m
[0m[31m## Step-by-Step Solution
[0m[31m
[0m[31m1. Read input: n, directions string, jump lengths
[0m[31m2. Start at position 0
[0m[31m3. Use a set to track visited positions
[0m[31m4. While the current position is within bounds:
[0m[31m   - If we've visited this position before → cycle detected → INFINITE
[0m[31m   - Otherwise, mark it as visited
[0m[31m   - Calculate next position based on direction and jump length
[0m[31m   - Move to next position
[0m[31m5. If we exit bounds, return FINITE
[0m[31m
[0m[31m## Edge Cases
[0m[31m
[0m[31m- Single cell: if direction is '<' or '>' and jump length > 0, will jump out
[0m[31m- Position 0: jumping right might go out of bounds
[0m[31m- Position n-1: jumping left might go out of bounds
[0m[31m
[0m[31m```python
[0m[31mn = int(input())
[0m[31mdirections = input().strip()
[0m[31mjumps = list(map(int, input().split()))
[0m[31m
[0m[31mvisited = set()
[0m[31mpos = 0
[0m[31m
[0m[31mwhile 0 <= pos < n:
[0m[31m    if pos in visited:
[0m[31m        print("INFINITE")
[0m[31m        exit()
[0m[31m    
[0m[31m    visited.add(pos)
[0m[31m    
[0m[31m    # Determine next position based on direction
[0m[31m    if directions[pos] == '>':
[0m[31m        pos = pos + jumps[pos]
[0m[31m    else:  # directions[pos] == '<'
[0m[31m        pos = pos - jumps[pos]
[0m[31m
[0m[31m# If we exit the loop, grasshopper jumped out of bounds
[0m[31mprint("FINITE")
[0m[31m```
